{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-73616" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The row echelon form matrix $P$ is given below. What are its **non**-pivot columns?\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069124/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab8e0dc41d40895a19b76b2ff951816aedebfc36a321b4805203642cc3613170"} {"question" "q-73616" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $P$ has $2$ pivots in the $1$st and $2$nd columns:\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only non-pivot column is the $3$rd column." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069124/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab8e0dc41d40895a19b76b2ff951816aedebfc36a321b4805203642cc3613170"} {"question" "q-73616" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069124/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4e0e1999bca372ed2125e853746557d3d12e0b2b1ff1de845e59ea5266418531"} {"question" "q-73616" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069124/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab8e0dc41d40895a19b76b2ff951816aedebfc36a321b4805203642cc3613170"} {"question" "q-73616" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$1$st and $3$rd only"] ["text" "$2$nd and $3$rd only"] ["text" "$2$nd only"] ["text" "$3$rd only"] ["text" "All the columns are non-pivot"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069124/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab8e0dc41d40895a19b76b2ff951816aedebfc36a321b4805203642cc3613170"} {"question" "q-73616" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$3$rd only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069124/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab8e0dc41d40895a19b76b2ff951816aedebfc36a321b4805203642cc3613170"} {"question" "q-73618" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The row echelon form matrix $P$ is given below. What are its **non**-pivot columns?\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 6 & -1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069124/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab8e0dc41d40895a19b76b2ff951816aedebfc36a321b4805203642cc3613170"} {"question" "q-73618" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $P$ has $3$ pivots in the $2$nd, $4$th and $5$th columns:\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 6 & -1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only non-pivot columns are the $1$st and $3$rd column." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069124/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab8e0dc41d40895a19b76b2ff951816aedebfc36a321b4805203642cc3613170"} {"question" "q-73618" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069124/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4e0e1999bca372ed2125e853746557d3d12e0b2b1ff1de845e59ea5266418531"} {"question" "q-73618" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069124/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab8e0dc41d40895a19b76b2ff951816aedebfc36a321b4805203642cc3613170"} {"question" "q-73618" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$1$st and $3$rd only"] ["text" "$1$st only"] ["text" "$1$st, $2$nd, and $3$rd only"] ["text" "$3$rd only"] ["text" "All the columns are non-pivot"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069124/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab8e0dc41d40895a19b76b2ff951816aedebfc36a321b4805203642cc3613170"} {"question" "q-73618" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$1$st and $3$rd only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069124/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab8e0dc41d40895a19b76b2ff951816aedebfc36a321b4805203642cc3613170"} {"question" "q-73630" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine the number of pivot columns of the matrix $C,$ given by\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069124/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab8e0dc41d40895a19b76b2ff951816aedebfc36a321b4805203642cc3613170"} {"question" "q-73630" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to convert $C$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $C$ has $4$ pivots, and therefore the number of pivot columns is $4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069124/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab8e0dc41d40895a19b76b2ff951816aedebfc36a321b4805203642cc3613170"} {"question" "q-73630" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069124/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4e0e1999bca372ed2125e853746557d3d12e0b2b1ff1de845e59ea5266418531"} {"question" "q-73630" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069124/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab8e0dc41d40895a19b76b2ff951816aedebfc36a321b4805203642cc3613170"} {"question" "q-73630" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069124/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab8e0dc41d40895a19b76b2ff951816aedebfc36a321b4805203642cc3613170"} {"question" "q-73630" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069124/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab8e0dc41d40895a19b76b2ff951816aedebfc36a321b4805203642cc3613170"} {"question" "q-73635" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine the number of pivot columns of the matrix $Q,$ given by\n\n$$\nQ=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 8 & -12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069124/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab8e0dc41d40895a19b76b2ff951816aedebfc36a321b4805203642cc3613170"} {"question" "q-73635" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to convert $Q$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 8 & -12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 8 & -12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $Q$ has $4$ pivots, and therefore the number of pivot columns is $4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069124/state.json" "file_sha256" "ab8e0dc41d40895a19b76b2ff951816aedebfc36a321b4805203642cc3613170"} {"question" "q-73635" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069124/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4e0e1999bca372ed2125e853746557d3d12e0b2b1ff1de845e59ea5266418531"} {"question" "q-73635" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Aca